menu "CEC persistence (NVS / persist-on-fault)"

    config CEC_PERSIST_WRITE_BUDGET_MS
        int "Persist-on-fault flash write budget (ms)"
        default 15
        help
            The persist-on-fault contract's binding write budget
            (firmware/contracts/persist-on-fault.md): on the power-fail
            trigger the gasp must complete ALL flash programming within
            this many milliseconds — the RAM tail + commit record only,
            never a bulk dump, and program-only (the persist region is
            pre-erased in normal operation).

            The default 15 sits under the WORST-CASE measured hold-up
            ride-through of the Hub Standard 4700 uF reservoir (owner
            bench 2026-07-15: ~26 ms @ 80 mA base, ~23 ms @ 120 mA
            typical, ~16 ms @ 240 mA worst case). Re-tests update this
            default together with the contract doc's table — this
            Kconfig is the single source firmware reads; never
            re-hardcode the number.

endmenu
